<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended May 28, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					    May 28 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.67   -0.167    +1.036</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     4.77   -3.634    +0.352</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	460.30   -1.224    -1.151</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 126.90   -1.200   -35.300</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.57   -0.018    +2.043</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Apr 97     Mar 97     Apr 96</p>
<p>M1					  69.62	68.47	60.17</p>
<p>M2					 391.14     391.44     391.13</p>
<p>M3					 503.50     505.61     478.75</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			April	 March</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-17.29	-16.80</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     707.80	705.60</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.66	108.03</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
